{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>וְהִנֵּה הוּא יֹצֵא לִקְרָאתֶךָ</b> (behold, he is going out to meet you) — That is to say, it is revealed before me that he will willingly speak on your behalf out of his love for you, even though I did not command him. <b>וְגַם הִנֵּה הוּא</b> (and behold, he) of his own accord <b>יֹצֵא לִקְרָאתֶךָ</b> (is going out to meet you) <b>וְרָאֲךָ וְשָׂמַח בְּלִבּוֹ</b> (and when he sees you he will rejoice in his heart), and he will not be jealous of you on account of your superiority in this honored mission. <b>וּמַה</b> (And as for that) which it was necessary to say to him, \"Go out to meet Moses in the wilderness\" (Exodus 4:27) — this was in order to inform him of the route by which he would come. And it is possible that Aaron heard when Moses set out from Midian, and he went out of his own accord to meet him, and afterward, on the way, he was told: Go out to meet him in the wilderness, for there you will find him."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:03:05.751983615Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}